Add a fast-memfuncs option.

A size-optimized build (-Os, or --buildtype minsize) swaps memcpy,
memmove and memset for byte-at-a-time loops, about 5 cycles per byte on a
Cortex-M33. fast-memfuncs keeps their speed versions, the ARM assembly
ones included, while the rest of the library stays optimized for size,
as fast-strcmp does for strcmp.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 2c8de0f41f..15b0d5e138 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -80,6 +80,11 @@ if(NOT DEFINED __FAST_STRCMP)
   option(__FAST_STRCMP "Always optimize strcmp for performance" ON)
 endif()
 
+# Always optimize memcpy, memmove and memset for performance
+if(NOT DEFINED __FAST_MEMFUNCS)
+  option(__FAST_MEMFUNCS "Always optimize memcpy, memmove and memset for performance" OFF)
+endif()
+
 # use global errno variable
 if(NOT DEFINED __GLOBAL_ERRNO)
   option(__GLOBAL_ERRNO "use global errno variable" OFF)
